      en: "Bhitargarh is an archaeological site in Panchagarh District, Bangladesh, dating from the 7th to 12th centuries CE. It features a rectangular earthen rampart enclosing about 25 hectares, indicating a fortified settlement. The site likely served as a regional capital under the Kamarupa kingdom or early Bengal dynasties. Excavations have uncovered coins, pottery, and stone plaques. Bhitargarh provides insights into early medieval urbanization in North Bengal and is protected by the Department of Archaeology.",
