      en: ["Gokul Medh is part of the Mahasthangarh Archaeological Park in Bogra District.", "The site dates back to the Gupta period (4th–6th century CE).", "The mound has a diameter of approximately 100 meters at its base.", "The height of the mound is about 15 meters above the surrounding plain.", "Excavations have uncovered over 50 terracotta plaques.", "The archaeological site covers an area of about 2 hectares."],
