      en: "Teota Zamindar Bari is a historic mansion in Manikganj District, Bangladesh, built in the 19th century by the zamindar Teota family. The estate exemplifies the fusion of European and Bengali architectural styles. It comprises several buildings, including a main palace with columned verandas and decorative elements. The Teota family was one of the wealthiest zamindar families in Bengal, playing a significant role in local economy and politics. The estate fell into decline after the abolition of the zamindari system in 1951. Today it is a national monument and tourist attraction. The buildings reflect the wealth and lifestyle of the zamindar elite. Restoration efforts are ongoing to preserve the estate.",
